        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मन",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मन — man — \"the mind; the heart, as the seat of feeling\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आज माझं मन शांत आहे. āj mājhaṁ man śānt āhe. My mind is calm today."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter: माझं मन (man). मनात, in the mind; मनापासून, from the heart."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मन (man) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit manas, \"mind\" (CDIAL 9822); Marathi keeps the stem and drops the final -s."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
